  "title": "One container per git worktree",
  "summary": "Adds `.devcontainer/worktree-container`, a POSIX sh wrapper that starts, execs into, names and stops exactly one development container per linked git worktree, plus a stub-engine test script and a rewritten section of `docs/development.md`. The container mounts the worktree read-write at `/workspace`, the main clone's `.git` directory read-write at its host path, and the shared `.git/config` read-only on top of it, so git works while branch and tracking settings stay host-only. Container names carry a checksum of the full worktree path, and `GH_TOKEN` is passed by name rather than by value.",
  "lenses": [
    "architecture",
    "data-flow"
  ],
